---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { relFor } from '../../lib/affiliate-value';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CategoryHub from '../../components/CategoryHub.astro';
import FeatureMatrix from '../../components/FeatureMatrix.astro';
import AffiliateDisclosure from '../../components/AffiliateDisclosure.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Donor CRM software for nonprofits"
  description="Donor CRMs compared by real price and database size, with feature charts and head-to-heads for every pair we cover."
  section="donor-crm">
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Donor CRM' }]} />
    <section class="prose" style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">
      <p class="kicker">Category guide</p>
      <h1>Donor CRM software</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The donor CRM is your database of record: every donor, gift, and
        relationship in one place. Credible options start at $39-$45 a month and
        most price by the size of your database, not your team. Plenty of small
        shops start on their donation platform's built-in records first, and
        that is a legitimate starting point.
      </p>

      <AffiliateDisclosure />
    </section>

    <CategoryHub category="donor-crm" part="table" />

    <FeatureMatrix category="donor-crm" title="Feature comparison: what each tool actually covers" />

    <section class="prose" style="max-width: none;">


      <h2>How to choose</h2>
      <p>
        Pick by who will run it, then price it over three years rather than one.
        For a first real database, start with
        <a href="/go/eleo" rel={relFor('eleo')}>Eleo</a> ($39/mo) or
        <a href="/go/littlegreenlight" rel={relFor('littlegreenlight')}>Little Green Light</a>
        ($45/mo): both publish their full price ladders, both bill by record
        count, and both are month-to-month, so a real trial costs almost nothing.
        Where retention reporting is the thing your team asks for most, or several
        people share gift entry, <a href="/go/bloomerang" rel={relFor('bloomerang')}>Bloomerang</a>
        (from $125/mo, unlimited users) earns the higher bill.
        <a href="/go/donordock" rel={relFor('donordock')}>DonorDock</a> is our
        editor's choice in this category: one plan at $500/mo billed annually
        ($6,000 a year, plus $3,800 one-time onboarding and 2% on gifts through
        its giving pages) with every feature included, unlimited contacts, email
        and text built in, and the ActionBoard turning the database into a daily
        follow-up list. It is priced as a consolidation instead of a standalone
        database, so price it against your whole stack; if you only need a
        database, the record-count CRMs above are the cheaper comparison. Membership and event-heavy
        organizations should demo <a href="/go/neoncrm" rel={relFor('neoncrm')}>Neon CRM</a>
        before buying separate tools.
      </p>

      <p>
        Two habits save the most grief. Clean your list before you migrate,
        since most CRMs bill by record count. And run a test import during any
        trial to confirm gift history and soft credits arrive intact; a demo
        with your own data beats a demo with sample data.
      </p>
    </section>


    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The first real CRM enters at <a href="/stacks/250k-1m/">$250k-$1M</a>;
        see the upgrades at <a href="/stacks/1m-5m/">$1M-$5M</a> and
        <a href="/stacks/5m-plus/">$5M+</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
